@startuml
title Staff-facing view navigation map (proposed)
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "VIEW-S-001\nStaff portal home" as S001
state "VIEW-S-002\nCustomers and travelers" as S002
state "VIEW-S-003\nTouristic product catalogue" as S003
state "VIEW-S-004\nSuppliers" as S004
state "VIEW-S-005\nTravel orders" as S005
state "VIEW-S-006\nAdvice and assistance" as S006 #E8F4FF
state "VIEW-S-007\nInventory" as S007

[*] --> S001 : enter staff interaction
S001 --> S002 : manage customers and travelers
S001 --> S004 : manage suppliers
S001 --> S003 : manage product catalogue
S001 --> S007 : manage inventory
S001 --> S005 : manage travel orders

S002 --> S002 : search, create, review, edit, or correct
S003 --> S003 : search, design, version, activate, or withdraw
S004 --> S004 : search, establish, review, or edit
S005 --> S005 : search, review, prepare, secure, or update
S007 --> S007 : search, review, procure, allocate, or reconcile

S002 --> S005 : review related orders
S002 --> S006 : assist customer or traveler
S003 --> S007 : review product capacity
S003 --> S004 : review product supplier
S004 --> S007 : procure or review supplier stock
S004 --> S003 : review supplied products
S007 --> S003 : review related product
S007 --> S004 : review related supplier
S007 --> S005 : review inventory allocation to order
S005 --> S002 : review customer or traveler
S005 --> S007 : review allocated inventory
S005 --> S006 : assist on order
S006 --> S002 : review person context
S006 --> S005 : review order context
S006 --> S006 : continue assistance or record handover

S002 --> S001 : return to staff portal
S003 --> S001 : return to staff portal
S004 --> S001 : return to staff portal
S005 --> S001 : return to staff portal
S007 --> S001 : return to staff portal

note bottom
  Primary navigation is resource-oriented; list/detail/edit are within-view modes.
  Procurement, catalogue activation, allocation, and order actions retain business semantics.
  Role guards are absent because authorization policy is unresolved.
end note
@enduml
